  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode:00CDDTC8H0000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "title": "packaging.md",
    "text": "The full packaging effort is done, with no open gaps: the rename to `packaging.md`, the 3-way workspace split, the `aperas` dispatcher, `identity.json`/`aperas.config.json` configuration (including two independent path roots), a real build-to-`bin`, and the explicit-start service redesign are all shipped and verified — see [Configuration](../design/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CDHSJQE8001), [Workflow](../design/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CDY7PGG0001), and [Distribution](../design/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CDW3R42G001). `kg:show <ref>` — a raw single-node inspection command, once tracked here — turned out to be a TreeView/node-rendering gap rather than a packaging one, and moved to `AperasKG/artifacts/archive/Aperas-treeview-design.md`.",
    "parent": "FolderNode:00CDBYV4BR002",
    "children": [
