  },
  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode:00CEA5M69R000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "title": "aperas-skill.md",
    "text": "Restructure in place rather than rewriting from a blank file. Every existing item was paid for by a live incident, so the content is the asset and the arrangement is the defect — a fresh draft would silently drop hard-won specifics that no one would notice missing until the incident recurred.",
    "parent": "FolderNode:00CDBYV4BR004",
    "type": "root",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8001"
    ],
    "path": "planning/aperas-skill.md",
    "fileHash": "11f5cca0188d9a9fd1352cdcbd712130eaede68327b31dcfdfbe7371bde3fe25",
    "lastTrackedAt": "2026-09-11T18:22:16.871Z",
    "ingestedHash": "11f5cca0188d9a9fd1352cdcbd712130eaede68327b31dcfdfbe7371bde3fe25",
    "lastIngestedAt": "2026-09-14T20:57:02.090Z",
    "projectedHash": "11f5cca0188d9a9fd1352cdcbd712130eaede68327b31dcfdfbe7371bde3fe25"
  },
  {
    "@id": "ArtifactNode:00CEA5MGZR000",
    "@type": "ArtifactNode",
    "title": "aperas-skill.md",
    "text": "The restructure has landed and has been revised five times since. `skills/aperas/SKILL.md` (reached by symlink from `.agents/skills/` and `.claude/skills/`) is v2: four levels — Philosophy, Orientation, Discipline, Mechanics — read top-down, with a scope statement and a worked example at each of the first three levels, and only current, verified items in the file at all. v1.1 repaired the vertical thread between the levels, v1.2 grounded the recall machinery in the philosophy that makes it non-optional, v1.3 widened the scope from graph edits to the whole session while replacing the mechanical read-side gate with a remembered consent question, v1.4 re-keyed rules to outcomes rather than to the verb or event that produces them, and v2 retired the inline status vocabulary, raised reading the shadow to the same standing as writing to it, added the upward direction to traversal, and moved the document's own past into the graph. Open Issues is empty; what remains is [trigger accuracy against a held-out split](../planning/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEDFKN3000A), still unmeasured.",
    "parent": "FolderNode:00CDBYV4BR002",
    "type": "root",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8001"
    ],
    "path": "history/aperas-skill.md",
